From: PocketBoot developers <noreply@pocketboot.org>
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] arm64: dts: qcom: tbx304x: minimal LK2nd handoff

PocketBoot-only boot policy, not a general-purpose board-port change:

Request the firmware framebuffer via lk2nd.pass-simplefb. LK2nd creates
the simple-framebuffer node and its no-map reservation using the actual
display geometry and format. Remove the static framebuffer and reservation
to avoid overlapping reservations and dependencies on native DSI PLL
drivers. The experimental command line preserves unused clocks, power
domains and regulators instead of taking native display ownership.

Keep the firmware-enabled LCD supply on during fixed-regulator probe.
Without regulator-boot-on, that driver requests the enable GPIO low;
regulator_ignore_unused only prevents later cleanup and cannot undo the
initial power cut. The native panel consumer is absent in this profile.
Retain the board's existing GPIO polarity and fixed voltage.

Use USB only as a peripheral for initial diagnostics. Drop the charger
extcon and host VBUS dependencies so gadget probing does not need the
SMBCHG driver or its battery/charging policy.
Expose the existing role-switch API so PocketBoot can explicitly request
device role for this extcon-free bootstrap.
That request supplies software session-valid state; peripheral mode alone
does not assert VBUS. This is a bootstrap workaround pending a proper
connector/VBUS path, not a general peripheral-mode requirement.

Keep the board port's remaining memory reservations and PSCI CPU method.
No RAM size or CPU parking protocol changes are added. Native panel
programming remains with the firmware.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8917-lenovo-tbx304x.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8917-lenovo-tbx304x.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8917-lenovo-tbx304x.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8917-lenovo-tbx304x.dts
@@ -43,25 +43,7 @@
 		#size-cells = <2>;
 		ranges;
 
-		stdout-path = "framebuffer0";
-
-		framebuffer0: framebuffer@90001000 {
-			compatible = "simple-framebuffer";
-			reg = <0x0 0x90001000 0x0 (800 * 1280 * 3)>;
-			width = <800>;
-			height = <1280>;
-			stride = <(800 * 3)>;
-			format = "r8g8b8";
-			clocks = <&gcc GCC_MDSS_AHB_CLK>,
-				 <&gcc GCC_MDSS_AXI_CLK>,
-				 <&gcc GCC_MDSS_VSYNC_CLK>,
-				 <&gcc GCC_MDSS_MDP_CLK>,
-				 <&gcc GCC_MDSS_BYTE0_CLK>,
-				 <&gcc GCC_MDSS_PCLK0_CLK>,
-				 <&gcc GCC_MDSS_ESC0_CLK>;
-			power-domains = <&gcc MDSS_GDSC>;
-			status = "disabled";
-		};
+		/* LK2nd supplies simple-framebuffer and its memory reservation. */
 	};
 
 	gpio-keys {
@@ -91,6 +73,7 @@
 	lcd_3v3: lcd-3v3-regulator {
 		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
 		regulator-name = "lcd_3v3";
+		regulator-boot-on;
 		regulator-min-microvolt = <3300000>;
 		regulator-max-microvolt = <3300000>;
 		gpio = <&tlmm 46 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
@@ -99,11 +82,6 @@
 	};
 
 	reserved-memory {
-		framebuffer_mem: framebuffer@90001000 {
-			reg = <0x0 0x90001000 0x0 (1280 * 800 * 3)>;
-			no-map;
-		};
-
 		ramoops_mem: ramoops@8ee00000 {
 			compatible = "ramoops";
 			reg = <0x0 0x8ee00000 0x0 0x80000>;
@@ -448,9 +426,8 @@
 };
 
 &usb {
-	dr_mode = "otg";
-	extcon = <&pmi8950_smbcharger>, <&pmi8950_smbcharger>;
-	vbus-supply = <&otg_vbus>;
+	dr_mode = "peripheral";
+	usb-role-switch;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
